  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multiprofile + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + concat (config_016, acc=0.5176) is the best configuration, substantially outperforming all singleprofile variants (~0.43). Within this top setup, we have only tested scgpt as the RNA encoder. config_010 isolates the RNA encoder choice by swapping scgpt → scvi_n200 while holding all other hyperparameters (multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) constant. This is the cleanest A/B test to determine whether the RNA encoder is a bottleneck or whether the current 0.5176 ceiling is driven by the aggregation/fusion/image-encoder choices. If scvi_n200 matches or beats scgpt, it opens a new optimization axis; if it underperforms, it confirms scgpt's value and focuses remaining budget on fusion/aggregation refinements. With 4 experiments left, resolving this key design variable is the highest-information next step before committing to fine-tuning the best pipeline."
